WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.200
Video twelve. Journal, credit note and debit
note.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.886
A journal records an entry without cash or a
bank.

00:00:07.816 --> 00:00:12.700
One ledger is debit, the salary. The other is
credit, Salary Payable.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.683
V opens the vouchers. F7 is a journal.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:22.935
Enter selects Dr: debit. Select Salary, and
type ₹40,000.

00:00:23.363 --> 00:00:29.112
C selects Cr: credit. Select Salary Payable:
Hisaab fills the same amount.

00:00:29.452 --> 00:00:33.068
Type the narration, and press Ctrl+A to save.

00:00:34.217 --> 00:00:37.501
A credit note: your customer returns goods.

00:00:37.431 --> 00:00:40.782
A debit note: you return goods to a supplier.

00:00:41.082 --> 00:00:45.966
Alt+F6 is a credit note. Select Patel
Garments, and the sales ledger.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:51.219
The item that comes back: 5 metres of silk, at
₹900.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:58.137
Select CGST and SGST: Hisaab calculates the
tax. Then the narration.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:06.123
Ctrl+I opens More Details. In Statutory Details, give the
reason and the original invoice: number 2 of 31 May.

00:01:09.271 --> 00:01:13.487
Ctrl+A accepts. Agst Ref takes the amount off
invoice 2.

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:18.258
The credit note is saved.

00:01:20.252 --> 00:01:25.338
Alt+F5 is a debit note. Select Mehta Fabrics,
and the purchase ledger.

00:01:26.037 --> 00:01:31.656
100 metres of cotton at ₹110, with IGST:
another state.

00:01:32.355 --> 00:01:38.104
Type the narration, and give the original bill
in Statutory Details: MF/101.

00:01:41.252 --> 00:01:47.136
Ctrl+A accepts. Bill MF/101 is paid already,
so the bill-wise details take New Ref.

00:01:47.166 --> 00:01:49.316
The debit note is saved.

00:01:51.053 --> 00:01:55.404
Patel Garments now owes ₹4,725 less.

00:01:55.334 --> 00:02:00.084
Mehta Fabrics now owes you ₹11,550.

00:02:00.283 --> 00:02:03.634
Next: banking, and the bank reconciliation.

